{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387950-m20-questions-about-casting-spell","id":1387950,"title":"M20: questions about casting spell?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-13T01:13:23-07:00","id":1387950,"title":"M20: questions about casting spell?","content":"Gathering info about the 20 anniversary edition I came up with some question about spellcasting rules:<br /> <br /> 1) To cast any spell you roll only Arete + bonus dice, it's correct? Don't you think it's a very minimal dice pool?<br /> <br /> 2) A difficulty spell refers to the target number or it's about the ammount of the successes needed to cast a spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T02:11:04-07:00","id":1387956,"title":"","content":"1) Bonus dice? Well, it is a small pool. While a few successes can go a long way, I think the pool was kept small to make magic inherently unreliable and force players to spend time preparing powerful spells as opposed to slinging them on the fly.<br /> <br /> 2) Difficulty refers to target number.<br /> <br /> Edit: Just to mention, despite the small pool for magic rolls, starting mages built and used right can be quite powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 05-13-2020, 05:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T02:39:07-07:00","id":1387964,"title":"","content":"You cannot attach any bonus dice to arete rolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T03:13:07-07:00","id":1387971,"title":"","content":"There are very limited ways to get bonus dice to Arete rolls, and those generally have further limitations to them.<br /> <br /> Ritual magic with non-mage assistants is the most common way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T03:46:56-07:00","id":1387973,"title":"","content":"So tools like rods and similar don't grant any bonus just like in Awakening?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 05-13-2020, 06:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T04:36:08-07:00","id":1387979,"title":"","content":"Not to dice-pools, despite their similarities, Awakening and Ascension have some very key differences; especially in how spell casting is constructed.<br /> <br /> Tools (foci in older editions, instruments in M20) are a base requirement for spells (at least at start), with more specialized ones reducing the difficulty of the roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:29:35-07:00","id":1388013,"title":"","content":"The main way to make magic easier is to reduce the difficulty and you can reduce it by a maximum of three. The dice pool is unfortunately small yes and this, I feel was to eliminate part of the power of dynamic casting. In awakening they realized that Arete only may have been too limiting and made the pools bigger. <br /> <br /> You can still do many things with Ascensions Arete only approach but many players focus on buying up there attention with freebies and XP right off the cuff which is unfortunate as this means many people spend there freebies in the same manor every time to get to Arete three. One house rule we have taken to of late is to just start our characters at Arete Two or Three and disallow players to buy Arete with freebies. Arete Two games feel somewhat streetlevel and Arete three feels more mage. But that is the way it fells to us and not necessarily to everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T08:04:09-07:00","id":1388049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387950-m20-questions-about-casting-spell?p=1387956#post1387956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Bonus dice? Well, it is a small pool. While a few successes can go a long way...</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait a sec, are you telling me that to cast a canonic fireball I may need more than a success and maybe more than a turn?<br /> What the hell is this!? If I'm facing a vampire do you think Mr Cainite will awaits two or more turns until I'm ready to burn him crisp?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 05-13-2020, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T08:17:04-07:00","id":1388053,"title":"","content":"Mage isn't really a game about lobbing fireballs. Certainly not for initiates: at Arete 1, you're also limited to the first level of whatever Spheres you have; and Forces 1 doesn't let you lob fireballs anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T10:45:48-07:00","id":1388089,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, if you have Arete 3 (and can reduce the difficulty to 4 and/or expend one WP for extra bang) lobbing a fireball with Forces 3/Prime 2 it's do-able. Because Forces adds one success to the damage, you only need 2 Arete successes to cause 6 lvls of agg.<br /> <br /> Still may not be the most efficient route if you're facing a vampire. It's certainly not the cheapest<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-13-2020, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T12:25:09-07:00","id":1388117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387950-m20-questions-about-casting-spell?p=1388049#post1388049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait a sec, are you telling me that to cast a canonic fireball I may need more than a success and maybe more than a turn?<br /> What the hell is this!? If I'm facing a vampire do you think Mr Cainite will awaits two or more turns until I'm ready to burn him crisp?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, generally yes, but with 3 dice at character creation, a difficulty of 7 or 8 reduced to maybe 4 or 5 by spending 3 Quintessence and the expenditure of 1 willpower, you have a decent chance of hitting someone with 9 levels of aggravated damage that can't be dodged or blocked. <br /> <br /> Now, if you had forces 3 spent 1 day rolling to make an explosion and do this for a week, sending 1 will a day, and only got 2 successes a day, you can like get 29 levels of damage in an area that very few beings can do anything about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T13:05:28-07:00","id":1388125,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that arete 3 is when you get to drop your first instrument. if that is from it happens to be the one that you use to throw fireballs, then using that instrument gets you a -1 difficulty right there. If you happen to be able to tap into a suitable Resonance, that's another - 1 difficulty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-14-2020, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T16:31:08-07:00","id":1388180,"title":"","content":"You can get bonus dice only if you're using Familiar Rules from Book of Shadows that you gain a bonus dice when with your Familiar, or if you using the Ressonance rule and once per Story you can boost your Arete for effects that goes with your Ressonance.<br /> Also, to cast a Fireball you need to expend a sucess to affect something that's not you, so with 2 sucess you can do 4 damage, 3 can do 6 and so (remember that using Forces give you a extra sucess of damage), if you hit 3 sucess OVER the amount needed for the effect the Storyteller should give you some extra damage. I guess you could bypass this 1 sucess threeshold if using Violence as focus.<br /> A Tremere need to roll to a difficult of 8 for doing 3 agravated damage at Lure of Flames 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26165,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26165-gothicxxx","user":"GothicxXx","date":". 05-13-2020, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26165-gothicxxx","name":"GothicxXx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T20:49:20-07:00","id":1388225,"title":"","content":"Also keep in mind that, compared to Awakening, each success is twice as potent or more. I noticed this when panning a Rote for a Sorcerers Crusade game I was in. Out of curiosity, I compared what would be needed in each game. Something I was able to accomplish with only 7 successes in Ascension/SC, I figured I would need fifteen to twenty to accomplish in Awakening. Or rather, I would need to deduct that many dice from my roll to reach the parameters required. Don't quote me, it was a rough at-a-glance estimate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T22:31:35-07:00","id":1388232,"title":"","content":"A small but notable rules change in M20 is that affects on others require at least 2 successes rather than an additional success. The first target is part of the package but you need 2 successes or the spell fails as opposed to you need x successes +1 for targeting someone other than yourself. When you look at the damage chart, you'll note that the damage for 1, 2, 3... Successes is 0, 2, 6, 8 ,10. Meaning at 3 or more successes, it's like you didn't waste a success targeting someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T05:39:02-07:00","id":1388304,"title":"","content":"I think the big problem is that you may need more than a turn to cast a spell. If you engage a fight with a foe, we can easily assume that your opponent is not going to sit down for two or more turns awaiting for your spell to be ready.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T05:54:09-07:00","id":1388307,"title":"","content":"Well, as a mage, if you run into a foe and end up in a fight on fair terms, usually this means you screwed up or didn't have a good enough escape plan. As I mentioned, dealing 9 levels of damage in one turn by spending 1, will and 3 Quintessence is possible, but if you are fighting something that can shrug that off, you really didn't prepare for the fight or to escape well enough. <br /> <br /> For example, with Correspondence 2 and maybe forces 3. You could theoretically create a walking, talking forces based illusion for you to remotely control and to attack things for you, from the safety of somewhere far away. <br /> <br /> With entropy 2 or 3 and high stats life 3, you could boost dexterity to inhuman levels after a few days ritual and have your difficulties lowered by 3, perhaps achieving something like 15 pool for combat with TN 3 for most things. Coupled with good weapons or just inhuman strength and stamina. <br /> <br /> And so on with other magick<br /> <br /> Sure most of this is vulgar, but by rolling all it's effects into a massive spell, you only take the paradox every few months.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T06:05:13-07:00","id":1388312,"title":"","content":"Its why the classic statement of Mage Ascension is that an unprepared Mage is a dead Mage. Whereas a prepared Mage is neigh unstoppable. \ud83e\uddd9","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T07:35:50-07:00","id":1388331,"title":"","content":"One of the most annoying things I've come across was a mind reader mage with boosted skills (most relevant ones at 5) and -3 difficulty to his actions related to combat, that imposed +3 difficulty on attacks or hostile action against him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T08:11:18-07:00","id":1388336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387950-m20-questions-about-casting-spell?p=1388304#post1388304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the big problem is that you may need more than a turn to cast a spell. If you engage a fight with a foe, we can easily assume that your opponent is not going to sit down for two or more turns awaiting for your spell to be ready.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quick combat spells will do enough damage with only one roll - as Aleph described - at Arete 3 and some effort. And 'enough' means 8 aggravated damage to soak with some little luck. If you manage to get to Arete 4 or 5, even spending WP or Quintessence becomes less of a worry.<br /> <br /> Also, there are several ways to prepare spells in advance:<br /> <br /> * Wonders of many types (Charms, Talismans, Artifacts, etc.). Especially Charms and Talismans can be potent.<br /> * Hanging spells with Time 4 - i.e. casting them in advance. Especially potent in M20.<br /> * Depending on St, starting a ritual in advance and doing the finishing roll in-the-field<br /> <br /> <br /> As people are saying, Mages are the most potent when they are *prepared* for stuff to happen. They are, in many cases, the weakest Splat when suddenly assaulted and the Mage not having any preparations in place or spells at the ready, so to speak. This is fine, because, as Tuch says - it's a thing of balance. A well prepared Mage is a force of reality-wrecking nature.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T11:05:05-07:00","id":1388366,"title":"","content":"You may also consider some House Rules for a slight bump.<br /> * Quintessence: instead of reducing Difficulty, each point adds +1 die to the roll.<br /> * Instruments: the first Instrument can affect Difficulty, then each <i>additional</i> instrument adds +1 die. Limit the number of Instruments to 1 + Avatar and attach a cost to learning instruments.<br /> * Rote Ability: kinda like Awakening. Or add the Sphere score if you know the rote (idea taken from The Enlightened Grimoire)<br /> * Rote die roll advantage: in lieu of an added Ability, knowing the Rote means that 1's do not cancel successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T12:46:37-07:00","id":1388396,"title":"","content":"There's an official rule about Abilities Enhancing Magick where an appropriate successful Ability roll can be used to reduce the difficulty by the number of successes; while it doesn't give you more dice, it's an easy way to hit the -3 difficulty limit and thus get the most out of the dice you have \u2014 especially if you have a Practice that's amenable to combining the two activities, like Martial Arts. (Think \u201cAvatar: the Last Airbender\u201d.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T21:41:47-07:00","id":1388560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387950-m20-questions-about-casting-spell?p=1388049#post1388049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait a sec, are you telling me that to cast a canonic fireball I may need more than a success and maybe more than a turn?<br /> What the hell is this!? If I'm facing a vampire do you think Mr Cainite will awaits two or more turns until I'm ready to burn him crisp?</div> </div> </div> </div> If you're accosted by a vampire while you're out and about, and the <i>sine qua non</i> of your making out of the encounter alive is whether you can successfully flambe the vampire... you got caught slippin'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T11:07:12-07:00","id":1390004,"title":"","content":"As other people have said, there are a lot of ways to prepare for combat ahead of time. Sustained effects are one of them--force fields, enhanced spatial awareness, physical enhancements, etc.<br /> <br /> One thing to wrap your head around in this setting though, is combat balance is not really a priority because combat is not the main focus of the game. Even if you have a lot of general preparedness, you'd probably get eaten by a werewolf if you didn't take them out in their breed form before they could change. Same if you're a vampire. Even <i>within </i>the different splats--if you're more combat focused you'll wipe the floor with others of your &quot;type.&quot; A vampire with 3+ Celerity for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","user":"Faradn","date":". 05-19-2020, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T16:17:42-07:00","id":1392070,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2457_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2457\" data-vbnamecard=\"2457\">Ipergigio</a> At Arete 3 you don't need more than a turn to cast a fireball like spell. And as others said, if you burn WP and/or quint you can do as much as 10 agg lvls. That's enough to send a vampire without fortitude (or even one with it) into torpor or final death.<br /> <br /> Now, you can take more than one turn and make you spell a lot more powerfull, that's what rituals are for. But that's harder to do in battle. Also, it is advised for every mage to have several defensive spell always active. Maybe casting them on the morning or giving them a nice duration. Since M20 does not have penalties for locked spells, you can have as much as you want. Just pick what best suits you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T13:11:48-07:00","id":1392886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387950-m20-questions-about-casting-spell?p=1392070#post1392070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it is advised for every mage to have several defensive spell always active. Maybe casting them on the morning or giving them a nice duration. Since M20 does not have penalties for locked spells, you can have as much as you want. Just pick what best suits you.</div> </div> </div> </div> Cannot agree with this more. People bemoan that it's a pain to have to do some kind of perfunctory casting every day, but the Light Sleeper Merit is only one point, and buys you a few hours you would ostensibly not have had otherwise (assuming your ST is good about enforcing the exigencies of a human body on the players).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T15:57:16-07:00","id":1392926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387950-m20-questions-about-casting-spell?p=1392886#post1392886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Cannot agree with this more. People bemoan that it's a pain to have to do some kind of perfunctory casting every day, but the Light Sleeper Merit is only one point, and buys you a few hours you would ostensibly not have had otherwise (assuming your ST is good about enforcing the exigencies of a human body on the players).</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you could just make them last more than a day. As long as your buff isn't vulgar you shouldn't get pattern bleeding","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T16:12:00-07:00","id":1393248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387950-m20-questions-about-casting-spell?p=1392926#post1392926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or you could just make them last more than a day. As long as your buff isn't vulgar you shouldn't get pattern bleeding</div> </div> </div> </div>Pattern bleeding doesn't care whether it's Vulgar or not. Only that you're twisting your pattern into something it isn't for an extended period. This is true if you're growing four arms, turning into a bird, or just buffing your Strength by 1 dot. The purpose of Pattern Bleeding as a mechanic is to stop players from stacking a bunch of successes on a huge ritual and then having functionally permanent extra dots in Attributes for no XP cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T05:14:48-07:00","id":1393398,"title":"","content":"@Bluecho: Regardless, the effects can still last a fairly long time though (much more than a day)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T07:24:02-07:00","id":1393416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387950-m20-questions-about-casting-spell?p=1393398#post1393398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Bluecho: Regardless, the effects can still last a fairly long time though (much more than a day)</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as your supply of quintessence holds out yes. Otherwise you start taking unsoakable lethal damage at a rate of 1 per day. And though I may be mistaken on RAW but I don't believe it can be healed through Magick. At least thats how we have always played it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T07:40:23-07:00","id":1393423,"title":"","content":"In M20 it's only ever been mentioned in this regard: &quot;an organism that has been radically altered by Life Magick (given new limbs or other characteristics that are not part of the creature's original pattern) suffers Pattern Bleeding, an inexorable quintessence leak that inflicts one level of lethal damage per day. Unless the caster uses Prime magick to refill that Pattern with fresh energy, or alters that pattern permanently, the damage continues until the subject dies.&quot;<br /> <br /> For further context, it's in the Life Sphere entry and not, in my understanding, related to other types of Magick, at least in M20.<br /> <br /> Edit: so the damage is not unhealable, can be stopped by using Quintessence and prime, or by crafting a permanent effect (this seems new), and seems only related to radical biological changes, probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 06-01-2020, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T10:23:18-07:00","id":1393465,"title":"","content":"Ya, pattern bleeding really isn't covered much in M20. We still used the Revised rules that covers it pretty well. If I remember correctly as far as pattern bleeding relating to enhanced stats it only kicks in if they are raised above 5. I'd have to double check that though. <br /> <br /> Honestly I don't have to much issue with stat increases at 5 and under. I don't find them game breaking due to most of the stories at our table not being combat heavy. Even then stamina enforced with Prime 3 to soak aggravated damage I find to be more feasible than persistent force fields and what not, and not problamatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T17:40:38-07:00","id":1393557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387950-m20-questions-about-casting-spell?p=1393248#post1393248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pattern bleeding doesn't care whether it's Vulgar or not. Only that you're twisting your pattern into something it isn't for an extended period. This is true if you're growing four arms, turning into a bird, or just buffing your Strength by 1 dot. The purpose of Pattern Bleeding as a mechanic is to stop players from stacking a bunch of successes on a huge ritual and then having functionally permanent extra dots in Attributes for no XP cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, only for vulgar effects. This can be concluded in M20 and HDYDT. Unless you are refering to Revised rules, then you are right.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar987_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"987\" data-vbnamecard=\"987\">Tuch</a> You're right. Only effects that are considered vulgar leads to pattern bleeding (like attributes above 5)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T01:15:09-07:00","id":1393591,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> is correct. Pattern Bleeding is caused by <b>any </b>alteration to the target's Life Pattern that lasts for more than one day, vulgar or otherwise.<br /> <br /> Vulgar alterations that are rendered permanent cause Permanent Paradox, and may cause Pattern Bleeding as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","user":"Thebian","date":". 06-02-2020, 04:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T06:25:08-07:00","id":1393614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387950-m20-questions-about-casting-spell?p=1393591#post1393591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> is correct. Pattern Bleeding is caused by <b>any </b>alteration to the target's Life Pattern that lasts for more than one day, vulgar or otherwise.<br /> <br /> Vulgar alterations that are rendered permanent cause Permanent Paradox, and may cause Pattern Bleeding as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. This is what I had thought but couldn't remember what the time table was. For some reason I thought it was a week but that didn't seem right then I never got a chance to look it up. I completly forgot about the permadox until you mentioned it though.<br /> <br /> Like I mentioned earlier. My table rarely deals with the raising of stats as its generally not needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":". 06-02-2020, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T06:33:10-07:00","id":1393616,"title":"","content":"Seems to be a big edition rules difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T06:36:10-07:00","id":1393617,"title":"","content":"Just found this in M20 under Life Sphere on page 516:<br /> <br /> As a result, an organism that has been radically altered by Life magick (given new limbs or other characteristics that are not part of the creature\u2019s original Pattern) suffers Pattern bleeding: an inexorable Quintessence leak that inflicts one level of lethal damage per day. Unless the caster uses Prime magick to refill that Pattern with fresh energy, or alters that Pattern permanently, the damage continues until the subject dies.<br /> <br /> At no point is vulgar or not vulgar mentioned, and I would take &quot;characteristics not part of the original patern&quot; to imply attributes above what has been paid for through character creation and XP. Otherwise, why raise physical stats at all if I can just use Life magick to increase them for free?<br /> <br /> This quote also leads to the idea that the damge caused by pattern bleeding cannot be healed with magick short of quintessence expenditures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T08:55:47-07:00","id":1393647,"title":"","content":"The rules on Pattern Bleeding and Permanent Paradox haven't changed much throughout all the editions of Mage. Even the rule in HDYDT for making a Pattern alteration permanent through xp expenditure comes from the Revised era.<br /> <br /> For anyone interested in a deep dive into the various rules, the spoiler block below contains numerous quotes.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b>Mage 1e</b><br /> Under the Life Sphere writeup, Mage 1e introduces the concept of Pattern Bleeding:<br /> <br /> <i>Aggravated wounds such as damage from Paradox Backlash or Pattern bleeding (see Improve Body below </i>[NOTE: It's actually Better Body]) <i>cannot be healed with Pattern magick and can only heal naturally with time.</i><br /> <i><b>Better Body:</b> By reweaving the Pattern of her own body, the mage can improve slightly on Mother Nature. Each success rolled enables the mage to increase one of her Physical Attributes, or her Appearance, by one point. The effect has a duration based on the number of successes, but cannot become permanent. After some time, the instability of the mage's new form will cause her Pattern to &quot;leak&quot; Quintessence. The mage will first suffer one Health Level of damage, and will subsequently suffer more and more physical trauma (i.e. Health Levels) as time progresses until she dies. This damage cannot be corrected or healed until the mage allows her Pattern to revert to its natural weave (losing the points gained in Attributes), and then can only be regained at a natural healing rate, not through Pattern healing. Normally, the damage accumulates at the rate of one Health Level per day, but if the mage frequently exerts the capabilities of her improved body, this interval can decrease to minutes or hours.</i> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Mage 2e</b><br /> Mage 2e basically rewords this, although it calls it Pattern Leakage.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Better Body</b> - By reweaving the Pattern of his own body, a mage can improve on Mother Nature. Each success rolled lets him increase one of his Physical Attributes or his Appearance by one dot. These improvements can exceed the regular five dots, but the Effect then strays into vulgar magick. The Effect has the usual duration; if the mage wants it to become permanent, he must pay experience points for the improvements or suffer Pattern leakage.</i></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><i>Pattern leakage is caused by a metaphysical imbalance between a mage's outer form and his True Form - what he is, versus what he appears to be. As time progresses, this leakage causes physical trauma (i.e., Health Levels) as the mage's body feeds on its own life energy in an attempt to sustain its exaggerated form. A mage with this syndrome is, in fact, a thaumivore (see &quot;Mythic Beasts,&quot; Chapter Nine). If he's skilled in Prime, he may feed his body from the Quintessence in his Avatar instead. When a thaumivoric mage exhausts this alternate energy supply (which commonly happens if he doesn't meditate at a Node), his body will tum back to feeding on his life.</i></span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mage 3e</b><br /> Mage 3e has the same rules and describes Permanent Paradox as well.<br /> <br /> <i>If a mage affects a Pattern and changes it away from its true nature \u2014 that is, increasing or decreasing Attributes or adding new characteristics that are not natural to the creature \u2014 then the subject suffers the phenomenon of Pattern leakage (or bleeding). Over time (once per day, sometimes more often) the creature suffers injury as its Life Pattern fights the changes, generally taking one health level of lethal damage for each gross change. A mage skilled in Prime can use Quintessence to offset this injury, but when he runs out of Quintessence (or if the victim is not a mage), the problem will set in again. The only way to overcome this Pattern bleeding is to alter the Pattern permanently or to remove the changes.</i><br /> <i><b>Better Body:</b> If a mage changes a Pattern beyond normal limits \u2014 increasing Attributes to legendary levels (six or more), adding totally inhuman features, fortifying to soak against aggravated wounds, etc. \u2014 the subject gains permanent Paradox as long as the changes remain. Usually Paradox is a problem only for mages, but other victims can suffer as well, especially when Paradox erupts near them. Such gross changes always cause Pattern bleeding as well.</i><br /> <br /> <b>M20</b><br /> As quoted above.<br /> <br /> <i>As a result, an organism that has been radically altered by Life magick (given new limbs or other characteristics that are not part of the creature\u2019s original Pattern) suffers Pattern bleeding: an inexorable Quintessence leak that inflicts one level of lethal damage per day. Unless the caster uses Prime magick to refill that Pattern with fresh energy, or alters that Pattern permanently, the damage continues until the subject dies.</i><br /> <br /> A number of other books from the Revised line discuss this in more detail:<br /> <br /> <b>Storytellers Handbook</b><br /> <i>For instance, a mage can, using Life magic, give himself better muscles. Usually this use is short term to give a temporary boost; the mage garners a small amount of Paradox and suffers Pattern bleeding because of the stress of altering his personal Pattern. On the other hand, a Master of Life might use magic to preserve himself beyond normal human lifespan, retaining youth and vigor for a century. This usage clearly violates the \u201claws\u201d of conventional human existence. Why doesn\u2019t the Master suffer Pattern bleeding? Because instead of temporarily stretching his Pattern, he permanently rewrites it. The problem is that he rewrites it in a way that reality doesn\u2019t accept, so he constantly has the looming threat of Paradox hovering over him. In game terms, he has permanent Paradox.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Tradition Book Revised - Verbena<br /> <i>Pattern Bleeding:</i></b><i> Short-term enhancements \u2014 those lasting for less than a day or so \u2014 are relatively harmless, though they can cause the caster to accumulate Paradox, depending on their nature. Longer-term enhancements, those lasting for more than a day, place a tremendous strain on the subject\u2019s living Pattern. In essence, the Pattern is forced into a difference shape and kept there against its nature. This causes the Pattern to begin to break down, literally unraveling and feeding on the Quintessence within it to sustain itself, a process known as \u201cPattern bleeding\u201d or \u201cunraveling.\u201d<br /> Pattern bleeding causes the subject of an enhancement to suffer an unsoakable level of lethal damage per day. This damage cannot be healed until the subject\u2019s Pattern is restored to its natural state. A mage \u2014 either the caster or the subject \u2014 can spend a point of Quintessence to offset this damage, feeding energy into the life Pattern to maintain it. This sometimes leads radically enhanced or transformed creatures to become thaumivores, parasites with a constant hunger for Quintessence to sustain them.<br /> <b>Pattern Alteration:</b> It is possible to avoid Pattern bleeding by creating a permanent alteration to the subject\u2019s life Pattern, reshaping it into a new \u201cnatural\u201d form so that it doesn\u2019t suffer from any strain. This requires a vulgar Life 4 Effect with a minimum of five successes, and the caster must spend half the normal amount of experience points needed to raise the affected Abilities naturally, even if he\u2019s not casting the Effect on himself. For modifications other than Abilities, the subject suffers Paradox.<br /> <b>Embodied Paradox:</b> Although it is possible to transform a normal human being into a virtual super-human using magic, such things are not a part of accepted reality. Life magic that enhances a subject beyond the normal limits of its species is always vulgar. Permanently enhanced creatures engender Paradox by their very existence. For each dot of an Ability above 5, and for each additional permanent enhancement, the subject gains a permanent point of Paradox, causing Paradox effects to be that much more severe for the subject. This is one of the reasons many powerful Verbena masters lived in Horizon, the Seasonal Realms or other places in the Umbra. Their super-human levels of perfection could barely exist on Earth.</i> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Convention Book Revised: Syndicate</b><br /> <i>Advanced Therapies are usually stable, coincidental Procedures, but agents should expect side effects, including Pattern Bleeding: one level of aggravated damage per day, the agent retains enhanced Attributes, unless he spends a point of Primal Energy.</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> Finally, <b>Blood Treachery</b> points out that becoming a ghoul can cause Pattern Bleeding and/or Paradox.</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There was also developer clarification on this in the Revised era (I think from Malcolm Sheppard, but I could be wrong. Here's what that said:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b><i>How do mages gain and lose permanent paradox?</i></b><br /> Mages gain permanent paradox through a variety of means, though usually it comes from direct body enhancement beyond human maximums (as distinct from indirect enhancement \u2013 an Effect that increases Stamina may grant permadox, but an Effect that simply increases soak through other means won't) through the use of the Life <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022</b> <b>Better Body</b> Effect.<br /> Increasing a stat beyond five, growing gills or wings, or any other change that's impossible to maintain without magic will grant permanent paradox. How much it grants is up to the ST, but a good guideline is probably one point per attribute dot above five and one point per miscellaneous impossible trait.<br /> Other ways to gain permadox include the Enhancements background from the <b>Guide to the Technocracy</b> and, of course, anything else that explicitly says it grants points of permanent paradox.<br /> Mages lose permanent paradox by ending the effect that granted it.<br /> Note: In addition, canonically, a Mage gains permanent paradox for every century of life they have lived.<br /> To summarise, you gain Permanent Paradox from two main sources:<ul><li><b>Type A:</b> Major Backlashes inflict it, and it never goes away without special scourging techniques.</li> <li><b>Type B:</b> Long term Pattern enhancement causes it. It goes away when the enhancement goes away.</li> </ul>The name is deceptive. You can get rid of Permanent Paradox.<ul><li>Masters of the Art has suggestions for getting rid of Type A. The one reliable method is to get it burned out in an Umbral quest to the Radiance. This causes intense pain and three dice of aggravated damage per point of Permanent Paradox.</li> <li>To get rid of Type B, simply drop any Pattern enhancement Effect that provides superhuman ability. These include:</li> </ul><ul><li>Life or youth extension magic.</li> <li>Magic that raises an attribute over 5, *unless* it is gained through Archsphere mastery and not an Effect.</li> <li>Life Magic that allows the mage to do something a human Pattern can't naturally do, like gills or infrared vision as a part of the natural form's abilities.</li> <li>Life Magic that gives the mage's Life Pattern the ability to soak aggravated wounds.</li> </ul><b><i>What is pattern bleeding?</i></b><br /> Pattern bleeding is a condition related to but distinct from permanent paradox. A mage gains pattern bleeding by maintaining a magical effect in conflict with his or her natural pattern. This includes increasing stats or granting impossible traits like gills or wings. (It's not unusual for mages to suffer from both permanent paradox and pattern bleeding simultaneously.) It is possible to avoid pattern bleeding from stat gain by swapping stat ratings \u2013 trading a dot of strength for a dot of dexterity would not result in pattern bleeding, while simply gaining a dot of dexterity would.<br /> Pattern bleeding is a binary trait \u2013 either a mage is suffering from it or not. There are no degrees of severity, although there were in previous editions. Quite simply, a mage suffering from pattern bleeding takes one health level of unsoakable (even to effects that grant a soak against lethal) lethal damage per day that cannot be healed unless the effect causing the pattern bleeding ends. This can be avoided by spending quintessence \u2013 a mage suffering from pattern bleeding can spend one point of quintessence per day to avoid taking the damage.<br /> Note that because its effects occur once per day, magical Effects with a duration of one day or less never inflict pattern bleeding.<br /> To make this very clear, you get Pattern Bleeding when:<br /> 1. You increase your stats (without lowering another stat equally) or add inherent abilities. This includes changing yourself to gain merits or eliminate flaws.<br /> 2. This change lasts a day or longer.<br /> If you satisfy both those conditions, you must expend 1 quintessence a day or take an unsoakable, unhealable level of lethal damage for each alteration that causes pattern bleeding.<br /> To summarise:<ul><li>Pattern Bleeding occurs whenever you enhance a Pattern beyond its basic capabilities, but not necessarily to superhuman levels. For example, increasing a mage's normal 3 Strength to 5 creates Pattern Bleeding. Increasing it to 6 creates Pattern Bleeding *and* Permanent Paradox.</li> <li>In other words, everything that causes Type B Permanent Paradox causes Pattern Bleeding but the reverse is not true.</li> <li>Pattern Bleeding is straightforward. The afflicted individual absorbs 1 point of Quintessence per day. If the subject lacks Quintessence, she suffers one point of aggravated damage. This cannot be magically soaked and can only be healed with Quintessence, though this requires no other magic. The afflicted (or Thaumivore) can absorb it from Tass or a mage who magically transfers it without using magic, but can't suck it from living things or directly from Nodes without special powers.</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","user":"Thebian","date":". 06-02-2020, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T10:14:15-07:00","id":1393663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387950-m20-questions-about-casting-spell?p=1393591#post1393591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> is correct. Pattern Bleeding is caused by <b>any </b>alteration to the target's Life Pattern that lasts for more than one day, vulgar or otherwise.<br /> <br /> Vulgar alterations that are rendered permanent cause Permanent Paradox, and may cause Pattern Bleeding as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I disagree. As was posted, in M20 we have this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a result, an organism that has been <u><b>radically</b></u><br /> altered by Life magick (given new limbs or other characteristics<br /> that are not part of the creature\u2019s original Pattern) suffers Pattern<br /> bleeding: an inexorable Quintessence leak that inflicts one level<br /> of lethal damage per day.' </div> </div> </div>So, only radically changes result in pattern bleeding. The books examples are new limbs. One can interpret &quot;not part of the creatures original pattern&quot; as something that does not belong to that kind of creature, like wings of an eagle, or any attribute above 5 (strength of a gorila).<br /> <br /> Then in HDYDT we have this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So long as the changes remain<br /> within the normal human range \u2013 between one and five dots<br /> \u2013 and do not <u><b>radically </b></u>and abruptly alter the subject\u2019s normal<br /> appearance (as it would if you suddenly turned a skinny dude into<br /> an underwear model), the alterations remain coincidental; if the<br /> changes go beyond the normal human maximum, however, or<br /> make other radical changes to a person\u2019s appearance (huge eyes,<br /> antlers, etc.), then the alterations become vulgar. </div> </div> </div>This set what is considered to be radically. Which seems to be related to vulgarity. So, if you make a str 1 guy go to str 5, then it is a radical change and it will be vulgar and dealing pattern bleeding. If it's something simpe, like a str 3 go to str 5, then it is not something radical, so it's coincidental and won't deal pattern bleeding.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T10:31:28-07:00","id":1393668,"title":"","content":"I see at no point that radical implies a distinction between vulgar and coincidental. I could use life to allow my lungs to breath gas fumes which would be quite radical yet be coincidental if the changes were not visible. <br /> <br /> It really comes down to, as always with Mage, what you want to allow at your table. Follow 20+ years of precedent or go with loose explanations from the M20 books. Power Games/Players will choose less strict rules (not saying thats wrong), where as others will more likely go with less liberal interpretations. Who cares, if it works for your group do it how you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T10:37:07-07:00","id":1393670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387950-m20-questions-about-casting-spell?p=1393663#post1393663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I disagree. As was posted, in M20 we have this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, only radically changes result in pattern bleeding. The books examples are new limbs. One can interpret &quot;not part of the creatures original pattern&quot; as something that does not belong to that kind of creature, like wings of an eagle, or any attribute above 5 (strength of a gorila).<br /> <br /> Then in HDYDT we have this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This set what is considered to be radically. Which seems to be related to vulgarity. So, if you make a str 1 guy go to str 5, then it is a radical change and it will be vulgar and dealing pattern bleeding. If it's something simpe, like a str 3 go to str 5, then it is not something radical, so it's coincidental and won't deal pattern bleeding.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">M20 specifically defines such alterations as &quot;</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i>characteristics </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i>that are not part of the creature\u2019s original Pattern&quot;. </i></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It doesn't reference vulgarity at all. It's quite clear - any alterations from the original Pattern cause bleeding. You can interpret that to mean vulgar Effects for your own game, of course, or decide that the word &quot;radically&quot; has some special meaning in a rules context. Your game, your rules.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The section you quote from HDYDT has nothing to do with Pattern bleeding whatsoever - it's just a discussion on what is coincidental vs. vulgar.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T11:51:16-07:00","id":1393680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387950-m20-questions-about-casting-spell?p=1393668#post1393668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see at no point that radical implies a distinction between vulgar and coincidental. I could use life to allow my lungs to breath gas fumes which would be quite radical yet be coincidental if the changes were not visible. <br /> <br /> It really comes down to, as always with Mage, what you want to allow at your table. Follow 20+ years of precedent or go with loose explanations from the M20 books. Power Games/Players will choose less strict rules (not saying thats wrong), where as others will more likely go with less liberal interpretations. Who cares, if it works for your group do it how you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just arguing for what I think the rules as written in M20 are about. I try to follow dumb literal readings of the source book in my games.<br /> <br /> With no context from sources outside M20, pattern bleeding, as written, only seems to apply to drastic changes similar to new limbs and changes to the pattern (things within the pattern I think could mean more or less fat or muscles, a tan, or perhaps or other stuff you could probably achieve without magic because that's how your preexisting life pattern could be made to react to it's environment without actual change to your genetic code). If absolutely any change caused pattern bleed then I think they would have just said so and saved a bit of book space and a lot of confusion. There's absolutely nothing about unhealable damage. Just continuous damage until eventual death (which arguably could be from something other than pattern bleeding).<br /> <br /> Therein lies my disagreement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T12:59:29-07:00","id":1393686,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar987_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"987\" data-vbnamecard=\"987\">Tuch</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2543_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2543\" data-vbnamecard=\"2543\">Thebian</a> You guys are missing my point. Telling me that I can do whatever I want in my table is no argument, as anyone can , and should, do that.<br /> <br /> We are discussing about the rules as writen and it doesn't matter if there were rules that lasted 20+ years that were different. Those are other editions rules, and if they are the subject of the discussion, then I concede.<br /> <br /> Now, regarding M20, the rules, as always are very bad writen. My point about vulgarity was that both definitions (being vulgar and being passive to bleeding) seems to follow the same concepts. I'm not saying that *all* vulgar effects will cause pattern bleeding. I'm saying that effects that are radical changes (which were then described in HDYDT) cause pattern bleeding and happen to be vulgar as well.<br /> If this will help, forget what I said about vulgarity. The thing is, M20 states that radical changes cause pattern bleeding and then HDYDT specifies what is to be considered a radical change.<br /> Anyway, buffing stats to human level (1-5) is not described as radical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T13:25:47-07:00","id":1393690,"title":"","content":"M20 tells you what a radical change would be - it's an alteration from the creature's original Pattern. That's all there is to it. It's very clear. The fact that HDYDT uses the same word isn't some kind of rules definition - it isn't even related to the topic at hand. It's comparing coincidental with vulgar Effects. If you want to interpret the M20 rules as suddenly stepping away from all the other editions on this front by way of a definition that is strung out over two books by virtue of a single word, go ahead. Like I say, your game, your rules. It's not what the book says, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T13:36:36-07:00","id":1393693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387950-m20-questions-about-casting-spell?p=1393690#post1393690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20 tells you what a radical change would be - it's an alteration from the creature's original Pattern. That's all there is to it. It's very clear. The fact that HDYDT uses the same word isn't some kind of rules definition - it isn't even related to the topic at hand. It's comparing coincidental with vulgar Effects. If you want to interpret the M20 rules as suddenly stepping away from all the other editions on this front by way of a definition that is strung out over two books by virtue of a single word, go ahead. Like I say, your game, your rules. It's not what the book says, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, the book is not very clear about what is considered &quot;not part of the creatures original pattern&quot; nor what is a radical change. It does say that only radical changes apply pattern bleeding and we also know what is considered a radical change. By your logic, a simple change of eyes color from green to blue would lead to pattern bleeding and we both know that's not a radical change.<br /> Remember that the &quot;not part of creature original pattern&quot;is a description under the radical change. By your logic, every change is a radical one and that makes no sense<br /> If you want to consider a change in eyes color to be radical and apply pattern bleeding in your game, suit yourself. Just don't tell us that it is writen in the book that such a change would lead to pattern bleeding.<br /> <br /> I guess this all will depend of ST interpretation, so we don't have much more to discuss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T13:47:03-07:00","id":1393697,"title":"","content":"I never mentioned eye colour. Don't put words into my mouth to shore up your own position. The book may not be very clear on what a change from the original pattern is, but that was never the argument here, was it? I was taking issue with your claim that only vulgar Effects cause Pattern bleeding - a claim that isn't supported. Beyond that, yeah, you should absolutely interpret it for your own game as you see fit - nobody will come along and tell you that's wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T14:55:02-07:00","id":1393699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387950-m20-questions-about-casting-spell?p=1393693#post1393693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, the book is not very clear about what is considered &amp;quot;not part of the creatures original pattern&amp;quot; nor what is a radical change. It does say that only radical changes apply pattern bleeding and we also know what is considered a radical change. By your logic, a simple change of eyes color from green to blue would lead to pattern bleeding and we both know that's not a radical change.<br /> Remember that the &amp;quot;not part of creature original pattern&amp;quot;is a description under the radical change. By your logic, every change is a radical one and that makes no sense<br /> If you want to consider a change in eyes color to be radical and apply pattern bleeding in your game, suit yourself. Just don't tell us that it is writen in the book that such a change would lead to pattern bleeding.<br /> <br /> I guess this all will depend of ST interpretation, so we don't have much more to discuss.</div> </div> </div> </div>LOL, the move to absurdity. In case your wondering, the change of eye color falls under &quot;minor changes&quot; described under Life 2. Definitely not &quot;radical&quot;.<br /> <br /> Patern bleeding is not a new thing to M20. The interpretation of it has been fairly consistent through the editions. Never has Life magic been intended to allow for prolonged changes to a pattern free of charge, whether they are vulgar or not. If you don't want to consider ability score changes as radical then don't, but I dont see where the rules have changed from the older editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T15:15:35-07:00","id":1393700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387950-m20-questions-about-casting-spell?p=1393697#post1393697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never mentioned eye colour. Don't put words into my mouth to shore up your own position. The book may not be very clear on what a change from the original pattern is, but that was never the argument here, was it? I was taking issue with your claim that only vulgar Effects cause Pattern bleeding - a claim that isn't supported. Beyond that, yeah, you should absolutely interpret it for your own game as you see fit - nobody will come along and tell you that's wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We can conclude that you consider eye color to be a radical change, since you are considering <b>any</b> change that was not part of the original pattern. The green eye was not part of the original blue eyed pattern. I might be putting words in your mouth again, but that was my conclusion, if you didn't meant that, then please explain what you understand as a radical change. And if you do not consider every change as radical change, then you are just agreeing with me, when I said that only changes that are abrupt (above 5 traits, wings, etc.) result in pattern bleeding.<br /> <br /> About the vulgarity, I toke it back. They are not directly related, but they seem to share most examples, as I posted bedore.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar987_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"987\" data-vbnamecard=\"987\">Tuch</a> Ok, if there are changes that are not considerd radical, then those are not affected by pattern bleeding. HDYDT explains that 1-5 changes in attributes are not radical, then they do not apply pattern bleeding. Again, the previouseditin had different rules for this, as for a lot of other ones","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 06-02-2020, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T16:25:58-07:00","id":1393709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387950-m20-questions-about-casting-spell?p=1393700#post1393700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> We can conclude that you consider eye color to be a radical change, since you are considering <b>any</b> change that was not part of the original pattern. The green eye was not part of the original blue eyed pattern. I might be putting words in your mouth again, but that was my conclusion, if you didn't meant that, then please explain what you understand as a radical change. And if you do not consider every change as radical change, then you are just agreeing with me, when I said that only changes that are abrupt (above 5 traits, wings, etc.) result in pattern bleeding.<br /> <br /> About the vulgarity, I toke it back. They are not directly related, but they seem to share most examples, as I posted bedore.</div> </div> </div> </div>You would be wrong to conclude that - I haven't given any of my personal views, only citing what the books say for clarity.<br /> <br /> Personally, I wouldn't consider a change in eye colour to cause Pattern bleeding. A change in a character's dots would, however, even if it appears coincidental and doesn't result in stats over 5 (and I would rule that stats over 5 would cause Permanent Paradox as well as Pattern bleeding, until removed). Pattern bleeding would also be caused by giving yourself Merits, additional traits (even mental ones) - anything with a meaningful impact on the rules that lasts for more than a day. But stuff like eye colour or hair colour? No. That would be shitty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T16:37:24-07:00","id":1393711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387950-m20-questions-about-casting-spell?p=1393709#post1393709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You would be wrong to conclude that - I haven't given any of my personal views, only citing what the books say for clarity.<br /> <br /> Personally, I wouldn't consider a change in eye colour to cause Pattern bleeding. A change in a character's dots would, however, even if it appears coincidental and doesn't result in stats over 5 (and I would rule that stats over 5 would cause Permanent Paradox as well as Pattern bleeding, until removed). Pattern bleeding would also be caused by giving yourself Merits, additional traits (even mental ones) - anything with a meaningful impact on the rules that lasts for more than a day. But stuff like eye colour or hair colour? No. That would be shitty.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lol. Ok. Then you don't consider every change as radical. Good, we both agree that simple changes like eye colors are not radical and does not result in bleeding. Now, why do you consider small attribute changes result in pattern bleeding? In hdydt we saw that human lvl changes are not considered big (radical) changes. How do you get to the conclusion that eye colors is small and buffing strength is big?<br /> I mean, if you consider any change as bleeding consequences, then both of them should have. If you consider only big. radical changes, then both shouldn't, according to the books. Don't get me wrong, from what I see this is your personal opinion and that's completely ok. But it's a house rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T16:55:33-07:00","id":1393714,"title":"","content":"If it has a meaningful effect on the rules, I'll impose Pattern bleeding. If it's just for flavour, I won't. That's all - there's no deeper reasoning <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T17:26:58-07:00","id":1393716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387950-m20-questions-about-casting-spell?p=1393714#post1393714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it has a meaningful effect on the rules, I'll impose Pattern bleeding. If it's just for flavour, I won't. That's all - there's no deeper reasoning <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, fair enough. But, the OP table might not want to follow that interpretation, so I guess buffs are a good choice against supernatural foes. However, I believe that the best tactics are to make it &quot;impossible&quot; for the enemy to attack. Turning invisible might do the trick, while you get more time to use other kinds of spells from a safe place. Or even tryin to paralyze the target. Both can be done within 1 turn with Arete 3, I believe.<br /> <br /> I wonder how would be the rules for paralyzing a garou with Forces or even Life/Spirit...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T18:01:31-07:00","id":1393718,"title":"","content":"I would favor starting combat with effects that don't target the enemy, just in case they have unknown resistances to certain types of magic. Invisibility sounds great. Sound/vibration dampening and smell removal should probably be part of the effect, just to be sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T19:30:35-07:00","id":1393725,"title":"","content":"I've always used forces for impeding movement as Forces 2 to rob momentum, with successes calculated as per the Damage/Duration Chart being used as the Strength score for a Grapple Attack vs the target. <br /> <br /> Was that a run on sentence?<br /> <br /> With Life/Spirit to paralyze a Werewolf you'd need a Spirit 3, Life 4 effect and they'd probably be considered to get magic resistance. I wont even begin to go in to the BS of those rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T20:17:32-07:00","id":1393729,"title":"","content":"A minor correction to my previous statement. <br /> <br /> &quot;I would favor starting combat with effects that don't target the enemy, just in case they have unknown resistances to certain types of magic... Unless I can cast spells at my enemies with impunity or have a decent chance of ending the fight with a single casting.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, I'd typically want an escape plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T21:28:48-07:00","id":1393738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387950-m20-questions-about-casting-spell?p=1393725#post1393725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always used forces for impeding movement as Forces 2 to rob momentum, with successes calculated as per the Damage/Duration Chart being used as the Strength score for a Grapple Attack vs the target.<br /> <br /> Was that a run on sentence?<br /> <br /> With Life/Spirit to paralyze a Werewolf you'd need a Spirit 3, Life 4 effect and they'd probably be considered to get magic resistance. I wont even begin to go in to the BS of those rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good way to rule. With Arete 3 you can get up to 8 dices without spending WP. That might be enough to stop a Crinos. Might...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T06:15:22-07:00","id":1393767,"title":"","content":"Well if your lucky on the dice roll ya. If I wasn't really clear the Successes I use for strength then are used in the opposed Grapple Roll. So ya, if you had 6-8 dice vs 4-8 for the werewolf at least your on common ground. <br /> <br /> Of course if you make the successes from Arete directly relate to successes in the Grapple Roll then i wouldn't use the Damage Duration chart, I'd just take the Arete successes for what they were.<br /> <br /> Either way it comes out to about the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}